1
00:00:00,841 --> 00:00:04,377
To learn how to hop,
you'll need a unicycle

2
00:00:04,401 --> 00:00:06,422
and something to hold on to,

3
00:00:06,454 --> 00:00:10,594
like a wall, a large door, or a railing.

4
00:00:10,618 --> 00:00:15,389
To start, get on the unicycle

5
00:00:15,413 --> 00:00:17,806
and put the pedals at the same height.

6
00:00:17,822 --> 00:00:25,418
[Music]

7
00:00:25,477 --> 00:00:29,117
Once you're on the unicycle
with the pedals at the same height,

8
00:00:29,165 --> 00:00:32,920
stand up to put pressure on the tire.

9
00:00:33,465 --> 00:00:36,386
Next, keep your hand on the saddle

10
00:00:36,410 --> 00:00:39,852
so you can pull the unicycle up to hop.

11
00:00:41,086 --> 00:00:44,787
So, to bounce, you press on the tire

12
00:00:45,255 --> 00:00:47,595
by pushing down on the pedals,

13
00:00:47,648 --> 00:00:52,405
and that pressure on the tire
gives you the bounce to hop.

14
00:00:57,516 --> 00:01:02,169
Once you've got the hang of it,
you can try letting go of the wall,

15
00:01:02,387 --> 00:01:05,457
the door, or whatever
you're holding on to for support...

16
00:01:06,184 --> 00:01:08,504
...and try hopping without it.

17
00:01:10,934 --> 00:01:12,900
Once you know how to hop on a unicycle,

18
00:01:12,949 --> 00:01:18,743
try out other kinds of hops,
like "freehand hopping".

19
00:01:18,767 --> 00:01:23,069
To do that, squeeze the saddle
tightly between your thighs

20
00:01:23,089 --> 00:01:25,914
to hold it in place, and hop.

21
00:01:26,910 --> 00:01:31,429
So, get on the unicycle.
You can hop normally at first,

22
00:01:31,453 --> 00:01:34,927
and then let go,

23
00:01:35,086 --> 00:01:38,396
squeezing the saddle with your thighs.

24
00:01:40,606 --> 00:01:46,632
Next, another variation
is hopping "seat out".

25
00:01:46,726 --> 00:01:52,303
For this one, hold on to a wall
or something that helps you.

26
00:01:52,453 --> 00:01:54,204
Get on the unicycle,

27
00:01:54,313 --> 00:01:58,818
pull the saddle out in front,
hold it by the back,

28
00:01:59,180 --> 00:02:02,422
and then press it against your thighs.

29
00:02:02,930 --> 00:02:04,858
And you hop.

30
00:02:05,139 --> 00:02:11,466
Once you can hop "seat out",
push the saddle a little further forward

31
00:02:11,662 --> 00:02:14,262
to make balancing harder.

32
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:18,196
Your turn!

33
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:41,163
[Music]

